{
  "_comment": "Component name or CPE -> purl of the project's upstream source repository, for components identified in firmware, root filesystem and binary scans and read from a Yocto build's records (upstream-purl.py). Those components arrive with no purl, a pkg:generic one, or a package-manager type no vulnerability or license database resolves (opkg, openwrt), so a tool that looks components up by purl cannot identify them. upstream-purl.py sets pkg:<type>/<namespace>/<name>@<tag> from this table, where <tag> is the release tag the upstream repository uses for that version. CLOSED list on purpose: each entry reproduces a release tag of the upstream repository for the versions it names, and a name not listed here keeps the identifier it has (a wrong repository or tag points at a different version, which is worse than none). Entries starting with '_' are ignored.",

  "_comment_fields": "names: lower-cased component names that mean this project. cpe: vendor:product pairs (NVD CPE dictionary) that mean it, matched when the name is not listed. purl: everything before '@'. version: the regular expression the normalized version must match in full; a version of any other shape is left alone rather than guessed at. tag: how the release tag is spelled, with {v} the version, {v_} the version with '.' replaced by '_', and {1}, {2}, ... the groups of the version expression. tags: instead of tag, for a project whose tag carries something the version does not (a release date): the normalized version -> its tag, for the checked versions only; any other version is left alone. normalize: suffixes removed before matching; 'release' is a trailing package rebuild count (-1, -r2; at most three digits, so a date such as -20230520 is kept), 'build-hash' a trailing build hash of 20 or more hex digits (kernel packages carry one), 'zero-sublevel' a third part of 0 removed (5.4.0 becomes 5.4) for a project that tags a base release with two parts. verified: the versions whose release tag the entry was checked to reproduce.",

  "replaceablePurlTypes": ["generic", "opkg", "openwrt", "yocto"],

  "entries": [
    { "id": "busybox", "names": ["busybox"], "cpe": ["busybox:busybox"],
